tatus"},{"t":"storage DELETE","q":"DELETE /v0/b/{project}/o/synthetic.txt","a":"204","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"storage GET","q":"GET /v0/b/{project}/o (query: delimiter, prefix)","a":"200 {prefixes, items}","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"storage GET","q":"GET /v0/b/{project}/o (query: delimiter, prefix)","a":"200 {prefixes, items}","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"UI config","q":"GET /api/config","a":"200 · project {project}, 6 services listed","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"read hidden","q":"GET /v1/projects/{project}/databases/(default)/documents/notes/hidden","a":"403 PERMISSION_DENIED: evaluation error at L5:19 for 'get' @ L5, false for 'get' @ L5","r":"d","k":"error","w":"Firenook's denial starts with production's text (\"Missing or insufficient permissions.\") and then names the allow that refused it, without the official jar's preliminary pre-read evaluation error (COMPATIBILITY.md rules denials; DESIGN.md, no preliminary planner)"},{"t":"read missing","q":"GET /v1/projects/{project}/databases/(default)/documents/notes/missing","a":"403 PERMISSION_DENIED: evaluation error at L5:19 for 'get' @ L5, Null value error. for 'get' @ L5","r":"d","k":"error","w":"Firenook's denial starts with production's text (\"Missing or insufficient permissions.\") and then names the allow that refused it, without the official jar's preliminary pre-read evaluation error (COMPATIBILITY.md rules denials; DESIGN.md, no preliminary planner); the failed condition's cause is Firenook's own text (DESIGN.md, runtime error cause text)"},{"t":"coverage after","q":"GET /emulator/v1/projects/{project}:ruleCoverage","a":"200 {rules, report}","r":"d","k":"behaviour","w":"coverage counts Firenook's one evaluation of each write, as the create it is; the official jar also counts its preliminary update check, so the write rule's visits are doubled, and its read rule shows the planner's undefined visits (DESIGN.md: coverage uses actual evaluator visits, never manufactured planner visit counts; the producer evaluates once; runtime error causes are Firenook's own text)"},{"t":"coverage html","q":"GET /emulator/v1/projects/{project}:ruleCoverage.html","a":"200 {byteLength, sha256, title, embeddedCoverage}","r":"d","k":"answer","w":"the coverage page is Firenook's own same-origin renderer that fetches the JSON report (DESIGN.md, Native coverage reports); the official page embeds the report: status, content type and title match"},{"t":"after reconnecting","q":"reconnect to the requests websocket","a":"history replay of 10 evaluations","r":"d","k":"behaviour","w":"reconnecting replays the ten retained evaluations in order as they were sent; the official jar's history had appended later line outcomes to five of them (DESIGN.md, Requests transport component: no synthesized enrichment)"},{"t":"hub locator","q":"GET /","a":"200 {version, origins, pid, host, …}","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"hub emulator map","q":"GET /emulators","a":"200 {hub, ui, logging, auth, …}","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"create export user","q":"POST /identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/projects/{project}/accounts","a":"200 identitytoolkit#SignupNewUserResponse","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"hub auth export","q":"POST /_admin/export","a":"200 {message}","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"hub export origin blocked","q":"POST /_admin/export","a":"403 {message}","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"first start","q":"firebase emulators:start (auth, functions, pubsub)","a":"ready after 18 s · hub 200, functions 200, auth 200, pubsub 200, ui 200","r":"c","k":"behaviour"},{"t":"restart","q":"start the suite again on the same ports","a":"ready after 18 s · hub 200, functions 200, auth 200, pubsub 200, ui 200","r":"c","k":"behaviour"},{"t":"restart hub readiness","q":"GET / on the hub","a":"200 {version, origins, pid, host, …}","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"second stop","q":"stop the suite (control run)","a":"clean, exit 0 · locator deleted, ports closed","r":"c","k":"behaviour"},{"t":"ui api config","q":"GET /api/config","a":"200 {projectId, experiments, hub, ui, …}","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"logging websocket message 1","q":"connect to the logging websocket","a":"info: Watching \"<suite-root>/functions\" for Cloud Functions...","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"logging websocket message 3","q":"connect to the logging websocket","a":"info: ✔ functions: Using node@24 from host.","r":"c","k":"answer"},{"t":"first stop","q":"stop the suite (origin-guarded run)","a":"not clean, exit 2 · locator deleted, ports closed","r":"d","k":"behaviour","w":"the stop after the origin guard refused an export is clean, exit 0; the official CLI exited 2 there, a fault the recording itself names (invariants originGuardFallthroughObservedInOfficialSuite, originGuardedRunExitedCleanly false), and its second, unguarded stop was clean"},{"t":"ui index html","q":"GET /","a":"200 {byteLength, sha256, containsRootElement}","r":"d","k":"answer","w":"the UI port's root leads to Firenook's own console at /console (COMPATIBILITY.md Hub/UI: Google's Emulator UI is not served since 0.2.0-next.3)"},{"t":"logging websocket message 2","q":"connect to the logging websocket","a":"warn: ⚠ functions: package.json indicates an outdated version of firebase-functions. Please upgrade using npm install --save firebase-funct…","r":"d","k":"answer","w":"no warning that package.json names an outdated firebase-functions: the official CLI asks the npm registry for its latest version, and Firenook reaches the network only for its own update check and unvendored Extensions (SECURITY.md)"}]}